  "generated_text": "To find the average (mean) of all 5-digit numbers that can be formed using the digits \\(1, 3, 5, 7, 8\\) exactly once, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of permutations of the digits \\(1, 3, 5, 7, 8\\):**\n\n   The total number of permutations of 5 distinct digits is given by \\(5!\\):\n   \\[\n   5! = 5 \\times 4 \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 120\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the contribution of each digit to the sum of all permutations:**\n\n   Each digit will appear in each decimal place (units, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten-thousands) the same number of times. We need to find out how many times each digit appears in each place.\n\n   Since there are 5 digits and 120 permutations, each digit appears:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{120}{5} = 24 \\text{ times in each decimal place}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the sum of the contributions of each digit in each place:**\n\n   For each place (units, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten-thousands), the contribution of a digit \\(d\\) is \\(d \\times 24\\) times the place value.\n\n   - **Units place:**\n     \\[\n     1 \\times 24 \\times 1 + 3 \\times 24 \\times 10 + 5 \\times 24 \\times 100 + 7 \\times 24 \\times 1000 + 8 \\times 24 \\times 10000 = 24 \\times (1 + 30 + 500 + 7000 + 80000)\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     = 24 \\times 87531 = 2100744\n     \\]\n\n   - **Tens place:**\n     \\[\n     1 \\times 24 \\times 10 + 3 \\times 24 \\times 100 + 5 \\times 24 \\times 1000 + 7 \\times 24 \\times 10000 + 8 \\times 24 \\times 100000 = 24 \\times (10 + 300 + 5000 + 70000 + 800000)\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     = 24 \\times 875310 = 21007440\n     \\]\n\n   - **Hundreds place:**\n     \\[\n     1 \\times 24 \\times 100 + 3 \\times 24 \\times 1000 + 5 \\times 24 \\times 10000 + 7 \\times 24 \\times 100000 + 8 \\times 24 \\times 1000000 = 24 \\times (100 + 3000 + 50000 + 700000 + 8000000)\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     = 24 \\times 8753100 = 210074400\n     \\]\n\n   - **Thousands place:**\n     \\[\n     1 \\times 24 \\times 1000 + 3 \\times 24 \\times 10000 + 5 \\times 24 \\times 100000 + 7 \\times 24 \\times 1000000 + 8 \\times 24 \\times 10000000 = 24 \\times (1000 + 30000 + 500000 + 7000000 + 80000000)\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     = 24 \\times 87531000 = 2100744000\n     \\]\n\n   - **Ten-thousands place:**\n     \\[\n     1 \\times 24 \\times 10000 + 3 \\times 24 \\times 100000 + 5 \\times 24 \\times 1000000 + 7 \\times 24 \\times 10000000 + 8 \\times 2",
